The plate is a square dinner plate, roughly 26 cm across. The image is about 460 px across the plate, so about 17.7 px per cm. The rice pile spans roughly 210 px by 280 px, or about 12 cm by 16 cm. It is irregular and not fully covering that area, so the footprint is maybe 100 cm². The pile is probably 1.5 to 2 cm thick, giving about 150 cm³. Cooked rice packs at roughly 0.65 g/cm³, which gives around 100–130 g.

Cooked brown rice has about 1.1 to 1.2 kcal/g, so 120 g is about 140 kcal. There may be a little oil, plus a few carrot bits, so I'll estimate about 150 kcal.

